abstract: >-
  Zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 formalization of known facts, elementary identities
  and finite computations about the Hantzsche-Wendt (Promislow) group ring,
  Haah's CC1 curve and the symmetric group S4, with a Rust core, a Python exact
  oracle, a WebGL2 studio and a preprint. Lean checks Gardam's unit in F2[P]
  and determinant data for its integer lift, shows that no sign lift of
  Gardam's support passes an 8-point determinant test (a necessary condition
  for a unit), and proves a monomial lemma on a rational parametrization of the
  CC1 curve. String operators, Ronkin functions, braid groups and monodromy are
  not formalized; the related values are numerical or exact computations. The
  unit conjecture is false over C (Gardam, arXiv:2312.05240); whether Z[P] or Q[P]
  has non-trivial units remains open. The title names topics, not formalized
  properties; see CLAIMS.md and ERRATA.md.
